{# Shared JSON response schemas for conversation components.
   Included by message templates so every peer, advisor, manager, and
   verifier prompt spells the exact JSON contract the same way.  A
   macro takes no arguments and renders the literal schema prose. #}

{% macro tool_call_schema() %}Respond to a tool request with a single JSON object containing `action` and `args` keys:
```json
{"action": "<tool name>", "args": "<arguments the tool expects>"}
```
{% endmacro %}

{% macro verdict_schema() %}When you complete your review for this phase, respond with a single JSON
object containing these keys:
```json
{
  "verdict": "approved" | "changes_requested" | "commented",
  "reason": "a short rationale for the verdict",
  "summary": "a two-to-three sentence overall assessment",
  "items": [
    {
      "file": "path/to/file",
      "line": "12",
      "severity": "critical" | "major" | "minor",
      "category": "<issue category>",
      "description": "specific description of the issue",
      "current_code": "the problematic code snippet",
      "suggested_fix": "the corrected code showing the fix"
    }
  ],
  "suggestions": [
    {
      "file": "path/to/file",
      "description": "improvement suggestion"
    }
  ],
  "praise": [
    {
      "file": "path/to/file",
      "description": "what was done well"
    }
  ]
}
```
If there are no actionable issues, suggestions, or praise, emit empty arrays: "items": [], "suggestions": [], "praise": []. Never include placeholder paths (e.g. path/to/file, src/main.py). Only include findings you can confirm from the files you actually read.
{% endmacro %}

{% macro advisor_turn_grade_schema() %}Respond with a single JSON object:
```json
{
  "grade": "impressive" | "amazing" | "okok" | "acceptable" | "whatever" | "don't do this!",
  "feedback": "a short note to the peer"
}
```
{% endmacro %}

{% macro advisor_phase_grade_schema() %}Respond with a single JSON object:
```json
{
  "grade": "impressive" | "amazing" | "okok" | "acceptable" | "whatever" | "don't do this!",
  "feedback": "a short note to the peer",
  "improved_prompt": "ONLY when the grade is 'don\\'t do this!': an improved version of the original prompt re-explaining the task; otherwise an empty string"
}
```
{% endmacro %}

{% macro verifier_schema() %}For a tool request, respond with a single JSON object containing `action` and `args` keys. When verification is complete, respond with a single JSON object containing a `results` array, one entry per finding with a `finding_index` and a boolean `verified` flag.
{% endmacro %}

{% macro audit_schema() %}For a tool request, respond with a single JSON object containing `action` and `args` keys. When the audit is complete, respond with a single JSON object containing a `results` array, one entry per record with these keys: `finding_id` (the exact ID from the record), `record_type` ("item" or "suggestion"), `status` ("resolved" only with cited proof the defect is gone; otherwise "open"; terminal records keep their recorded status), and `reasoning` (non-empty; cite the file read and the reproduction or acceptance result).
{% endmacro %}

{% macro suggestions_praise_schema() %}Provide architectural improvement suggestions and praise for this pull request based on your exploration:

- **suggestions**: Non-blocking improvements to architectural style and design — such as reducing code size, improving class composition, extracting abstractions, simplifying control flow, or decoupling modules. (Do NOT report bugs or duplicates of issues).
- **praise**: Highlight specifically where this pull request excelled — good patterns, clean abstractions, solid error handling, effective testing, or elegant design.
- A concrete suggestion `file` may be changed in this pull request or any
  existing repository file that is directly or indirectly related to a changed
  file through a dependency, importer, caller, callee, configuration, wiring,
  or another traced architectural relationship.
- Before emitting an unchanged-file citation, inspect the changed file and the
  target file with the exploration tools and trace their relationship. The
  suggestion description MUST name the changed file or files and explain the
  direct or indirect relationship. An unchanged file without demonstrated
  relationship evidence is not a valid suggestion target.
- A repository-wide architectural improvement with no single target file uses
  an empty `file`.

Respond with a single JSON object containing `suggestions` and `praise` keys:
```json
{
  "suggestions": [
    {
      "file": "path/to/file",
      "description": "Concrete architectural improvement (e.g. composition, reducing code size, decoupling)"
    }
  ],
  "praise": [
    {
      "file": "path/to/file",
      "description": "Specific praise highlighting what was done well"
    }
  ]
}
```
If there are no suggestions or praise, emit empty arrays: "suggestions": [], "praise": []. Never include placeholder paths.
{% endmacro %}